/*
 * HISTORY
 * $Log:	task.c,v $
 * Revision 2.27  93/11/17  17:28:56  dbg
 * 	Rewrote task_terminate to iterate once down the list of threads
 * 	in the task.  Removed the call to thread_block() in the thread
 * 	termination loop and replaced with logic added earlier
 * 	(21-Jun-88) but lost in a later merge:
 * 
 * 	> Loop in task_terminate to terminate threads was incorrect; if
 * 	> another component of the system had a reference to the thread,
 * 	> the thread would remain in the thread_list for the task, and the
 * 	> loop would never terminate.  Rewrote it to run down the list
 * 	> like task_hold: take a reference to each thread, and release
 * 	> the reference on the next iteration of the loop.
 * 
 * 	When the current thread is in the task being terminated,
 * 	task_terminate uses thread_terminate to prepare the current
 * 	thread for termination, but not actually terminate it.
 * 	[93/08/26            dbg]
 * 
 * 	Changed termination protocol to simultaneously clear 'active'
 * 	and remove task port association.
 * 	[93/07/12            dbg]
 * 
 * 	Added separate task_ref_lock to simplify interactions between
 * 	task locks and processor set locks.
 * 	[93/06/10            dbg]
 * 
 * 	Break up thread lock, to simplify interactions between thread
 * 	lock and processor set lock and to reduce the amount of code
 * 	that runs with interrupts blocked.  There are now three locks:
 * 	. thread_ref_lock	locks the reference count
 * 	. thread_sched_lock	locks fields involved with scheduling
 * 				state machine
 * 	. thread_lock		locks everything else.
 * 	[93/05/26            dbg]
 * 
 * 	Removed priority field.  New threads are set to the
 * 	processor set's default policy (timesharing or background)
 * 	and can be changed after creation.
 * 
 * 	Converted time_values to time_specs, internally.  task_info still
 * 	returns time_values.
